 The domination polynomial packages dominating set information in a way that parallels several other graph polynomials. The independence polynomial counts independent sets by size, while the domination polynomial counts hitting sets for closed neighborhoods. Matching polynomials and independence polynomials often exhibit strong analytic phenomena (real-rootedness, log-concavity, sharp zero-free regions) that can be leveraged for coefficient questions. Domination polynomials are less rigid, but their coefficient sequences still appear to have robust shape. One reason is that domi
