ks: exterior Herglotz formula and uniform derivative bound for convex exterior maps; branch/log sign; strong L2 convergence and identification of limiting h and q on a nonsmooth convex body; normal-family inverse map and boundary parametrization; bounded fixed singular-pair Faber normalization when analytic domains shrink; exact full coefficient/positive-block residual signs; nonlinear H^(1/2) passage vs traceL1; totally isotropic subspace inference and inertia count; existence of simple top eigenvalue and positive-curvature analytic arc for irreducible sizes<=4; passage from a.e. slack to a point of that arc; tensor convention of rank-one X,Y and coefficient scalarization; irreducible-block reduction preserving normalization and excluding boundary spectrum; external scalar Jin theorem hypotheses and polynomial monomial deduction that controls outer summands. The parent independently checked the dimension4 anticommuting-involution calculation but has not approved the complete proof. Do not claim general nonattained psi_cb=2 or quantitative stability. Return PASS/REPAIRABLE/FAIL/UNRESOLVED, complete repairs "}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/astra-discrete-r2/discovery.md", "line": 65, "text": "- [Leake\u2013Ryder](https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.02499), Theorem1.7 and Proposition3.6;"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/root-hoggatt-r1/discovery.md", "line": 65, "text": "- [Leake\u2013Ryder](https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.02499), Theorem1.7 and Proposition3.6;"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/root-hoggatt-r1/preliminary-review-hashes.json", "line": 46, "text": "  \"sources/leake-ryder.html\": \"092598b0b33a39011d4a696ec3bb238d5ee0bad11dabd3f116ae5fc864fd124b\","}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/root-hoggatt-r1/preliminary-review-hashes.json", "line": 47, "text": "  \"sources/leake-ryder.txt\": \"8d18e4a694f72f3e20b72ca8d5587e1508431eebc5feafe7f4ed2ffb573e1fe3\","}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r30/discovery.md", "line": 1, "text": "# Fresh full-source target: Xie\u2013Xu 2-matroid ultra-log-concavity"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r30/discovery.md", "line": 7, "text": "Primary: Yan-Ting Xie and Shou-Jun Xu, *Ultra log-concavity and real-rootedness of dependence polynomials*, Electronic Journal of Combinatorics 33(4) (2026), #P4.9, DOI https://doi.org/10.37236/13310. The actual downloaded published PDF has 20 pages; its final source statements are on printed pp17\u201319. This differs from the arXiv metadata's 16-page description. The latest observed arXiv revision is https://arxiv.org/html/2408.09152v2, 10 October 2026; actual published body and v2 final-section bodies were read and compared. Publication landing page gives 9 October 2026. There is no forthcoming-resolution announcement located in the read source body or bounded follow-up searches."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r30/discovery.md", "line": 27, "text": "Important early public counterpart: Alex Chengyu Li's public primary project page https://crabresearch.com/research/augmentation-gap-log-concavity?lang=en describes a September2026 refutation of the OLD rank-dependent Xie\u2013Xu Conjecture4.8. Its reported construction has augmentation parameter THREE and rank4; this does not refute the surviving parameter-TWO conjecture. Source page metadata changed between indexed and current responses: current read lists SSRN, revised18September2026, DOI10.2139/ssrn.7434141; the indexed result listed Zenodo/revised8September. The linked body was inaccessible, and direct project/SSRN requests returned403. No alternate-host bypass or repeated challenge requests. Accordingly this is a material UNREAD-BODY prior-art gap, not definitive clearance for Conjecture17. No old rank-dependent extension is nominated or rediscovered."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r30/discovery.md", "line": 68, "text": "registry-screen.json preserves exact tree inputs and broad matches. Broad lexical matches such as independent-rate or matroid-matching paths are NOT matching actual proof claims; no such path is called a subsumer without reading its mathematical body. No exact dependence-polynomial/2-matroid endpoint path was identified. Fresh public exact-title, author-follow-up, conjecture and registry-index searches located the old Li counterpart above but no verified full parameter-two solution. Absence of path/search results is not novelty evidence."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r30/SUMMARY.md", "line": 3, "text": "Fresh selected target: Xie\u2013Xu, published EJC33(4)(2026)#P4.9 Conjecture17(iii), latest arXiv2408.09152v2 Conjecture4.4(iii): ultra-log-concavity for every finite additive-gap2-matroid. Includes the entire all-graph dependence-polynomial Conjecture14/4.1. Actual published pp17\u201319 and current v2 definitions/conjectures read. No full proof or genuine source counterexample found."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r52/discovery.md", "line": 7, "text": "One primary open-question paper screened: Jonathan Leake\u2013Maryam Mohammadi Yekta, *Log-concavity and Approximate Counting for Totally Unimodular Polytopes*, arXiv:2609.39917v1, 30 September 2026. Current abstract history fetched 29 October 2026 15:12 UTC lists v1 only. Actual HTML Question 1.7, definitions preceding \u00a73, and Theorem 3.1/Lemmas 3.2\u20133.4/proof read before diagnostics. Exact source bytes and URLs are in http.jsonl. No journal version asserted."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r52/SUMMARY.md", "line": 3, "text": "Selected one fresh primary target: Leake\u2013Mohammadi Yekta2609.39917v1 Question1.7, global geometric-mean inequality for all unimodular nonnegative integer fibers and all integer-mean demand distributions. Actual source statement and midpoint proof bodies read before investment. Current closest Schubr edition4 actual theorem/transfer proof body already claims central fiber dimension<=3; those cases excluded."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r59/discovery.md", "line": 48, "text": "A second conceivable generic route views M_lambda as the independence polynomial of the cell-conflict graph: two cells conflict if they share a row or column or one is SE of the other. This identification is exact. The graph is not always claw-free: in lambda=(4,4,4,4), center (1,1) and leaves (2,4),(3,3),(4,2) induce K1,3. Therefore the blanket claw-free independence-polynomial theorem does not apply directly. This does not disprove Ferrers real-rootedness."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r68/discovery.md", "line": 17, "text": "For every positive integer n, let G_n have vertices the nonzero zero divisors of Z/nZ, with distinct a,b adjacent exactly when n divides ab. Put s_k=# independent k-subsets, including s_0=1. The source asks whether the entire sequence s_0,...,s_alpha is unimodal. The empty graph cases have polynomial 1; no endpoint loophole is being used. This is the ordinary independence polynomial, not an independent domination polynomial, and not a statement about only selected gcd classes."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r68/discovery.md", "line": 33, "text": "For A subset D_n define F_A as the independence polynomial of its whole-class induced graph. For d in A, let N(d)={e in A\\{d}:n|de}. Then"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r68/SUMMARY.md", "line": 3, "text": "Screened three distinct graph-counting questions. Lee\u2013Seo Conj1.3 is excluded by actual successor2608.17920v1 Thms1.1/1.2; the W2 threshold conjecture is excluded by Pereyra2605.14076v1 Thms4.1/5.1 and full proof bodies. Selected Rather2606.04789v1 Conjecture1: ordinary independence-polynomial unimodality for every Z_n. Latest observed source is v1; source formulas and 2024 independent-domination counterexamples were read and distinguished. No older related campaign-summary hit found for375092/2606.04789 in the bounded local search."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r76/discovery.md", "line": 15, "text": "independence polynomials; squared-radius convolution; edge-irregulator;"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r77/discovery.md", "line": 9, "text": "Actual first-campaign record read before investment: 2026-10-26/new-discoveries/lanes/pi-euler-turan-final-review/fresh/trureturing/Problems/liang-sagan-2026-pinnacle-middle-order.md. It gives a public all-n>=6 no-upper-bound refutation of Liang\u2013Sagan Question 8.6(a). Do not rediscover it. The corresponding Library/Words/shankar2026canon.md and current pinned Lean body were read: they concern Canon-permutation Q moments, not the present poset. The first-campaign r40 working file was read and concerns metric Blaschke, an unrelated broad-keyword hit. r23 discovery says the old Shankar Eulerian real-rootedness lead has prior-resolution indications. r52 SUMMARY and discovery identify the already-investigated Leake\u2013Mohammadi Yekta Question 1.7; do not reopen it as fresh."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r77/discovery.md", "line": 11, "text": "Three initial source leads were screened at author/source level: Liang\u2013Sagan 2408.02782v2, Leake\u2013Mohammadi Yekta 2609.39917v1, and Shankar 2508.12467v1. The first two fail freshness for the indicated targets; powered Eulerian real-rootedness is publicly resolved. Only one new question received sustained work: the distinct order-theoretic Conjecture 1 in Shankar 2609.15651v1. This is not an accepted-family variant, and no claim of new-to-literature status is made."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r80/discovery.md", "line": 11, "text": "1. Leake\u2013Mohammadi Yekta 2609.39917v1 Q1.7: general integer-mean fiber-count geometric-mean inequality. Actual statement read, then filename-first all-date duplicate gate identified r52, confirmed in r77. Excluded before mathematical investment."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r80/SUMMARY.md", "line": 3, "text": "Selected Celano\u2013Elder\u2013Hadaway\u2013Harris\u2013Martin\u2013Priestley\u2013Udell arXiv2507.07243v2 Conjecture6.5: unimodality of counts of parking functions by maximum individual displacement. Actual latest primary statements and relevant proof bodies read. Leake\u2013Mohammadi Yekta Q1.7 was excluded early as r52/r77 duplicate; neighboring inversion bound and Foata assertion were screened out as routine structural consequences."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r82/discovery.md", "line": 14, "text": "is renamed as fresh. The initial broad independence-polynomial search was"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r85/discovery.md", "line": 7, "text": "Initial all-date report-filename gates precede source investment: duplicate-early.txt, duplicate-candidates.txt, duplicate-refined.txt, duplicate-final.txt. Searches include SUMMARY, FINDINGS, discovery and provenance reports throughout openai-proof-research, not just this batch. Relevant actual r68 and r59 report sections were read. The initial generic independence-polynomial screen encountered the old Rather family and was abandoned; r59 identifies the old Ferrers-rook family and an already public multiset rook-Eulerian refutation. No absence of a filename is treated as priority evidence. r83 group-Zagreb and all specifically prohibited targets were skipped."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-dewitt-rank-preliminary-review-r1/frozen/discovery.md", "line": 14, "text": "is renamed as fresh. The initial broad independence-polynomial search was"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-silicosis-multiplicity-preliminary-review-r1/frozen/discovery.md", "line": 15, "text": "independence polynomials; squared-radius convolution; edge-irregulator;"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r68/sources/lee-proof.txt", "line": 592, "text": ". Further work in this direction includes results for the independence polynomial and arbitrary degree sequences "}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r68/sources/lee-proof.txt", "line": 1429, "text": "The vertex-inhomogeneous formulation also provides a variety of examples. It captures multivariate independence polynomials, weighted list-homomorphism and list-coloring problems, and spin systems with vertex-dependent external fields."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r68/sources/lee-proof.txt", "line": 20343, "text": "Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r40/sources/input-5-SUMMARY.md", "line": 3, "text": "Fresh selected target: Xie\u2013Xu, published EJC33(4)(2026)#P4.9 Conjecture17(iii), latest arXiv2408.09152v2 Conjecture4.4(iii): ultra-log-concavity for every finite additive-gap2-matroid. Includes the entire all-graph dependence-polynomial Conjecture14/4.1. Actual published pp17\u201319 and current v2 definitions/conjectures read. No full proof or genuine source counterexample found."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-26/new-discoveries/lanes/pi-discrete-discovery-r7/FINDINGS.md", "line": 70, "text": "Open per the latest source I can see (Xie\u2013Feng\u2013Xu arXiv:2303.14671: \"the"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/matrix-disk-contribution-r1/review.md", "line": 66, "text": "R016, accepted, states the disk and a constant scalar channel \\(p(z)=v^*Pu\\) for every specified equality witness through base dimension four. Its rank step uses a simple top support eigenvalue, rank \\(d-1\\) of the positive boundary field, and the isotropic bound on \\(XX^*-YY^*\\). I245 records that this exterior limit and residual extraction are dimension-independent, and that the dimension enters only in the simple-support step. The parent note `crouzeix-five/analysis.md` replaces that step in dimension five by Leake\u2013Lins\u2013Spitkovsky, Theorem 5.7, and keeps the same scalar channel. The note labels itself a technical deduction and asks for no new-result credit. This review agrees. It is not recounted."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/kn-minus-edge-parent/proof-r1-input-campaign.md", "line": 92, "text": "  by combining the existing R016 argument with Leake\u2013Lins\u2013Spitkovsky's"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/artin-root-parent/r2-ledger-snapshot.md", "line": 92, "text": "  by combining the existing R016 argument with Leake\u2013Lins\u2013Spitkovsky's"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/coulomb-positive-parent/r2-ledger-snapshot.md", "line": 92, "text": "  by combining the existing R016 argument with Leake\u2013Lins\u2013Spitkovsky's"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/kn-minus-edge-manuscript-review-r2/review.md", "line": 73, "text": "**O1, low severity \u2014 `RIGHTS.md:9`.** Its inherited sentence says the survey extraction `work/chn-v5.txt` is present in this directory. The r2 README correctly says that scratch was omitted, and inspection confirms its absence. A future documentation cleanup can identify the location as historical r1 scratch or remove the exception. The public boundary is already correct and no third-party bytes leaked, so this does not block PASS_REVISION."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/expanded-target-2026-10-17/structural-r176-proof-r1-brief.txt", "line": 408, "text": "The new assertion is algorithmic: an explicit zero-error expected-polynomial algorithm for the source's full unrestricted graph class. Source181 gives the existence theorem and all structural vertex savings. BM supplies genuine expansion, sampling and iterative path/cycle machinery. CFS already supplies greedy saturation. Lovasz supplies the constructive path operation. Short-cycle algorithms, including LSY, already supply fast explicit partitions with a linear number of leftover edges; they do not bound the total number of cycle parts linearly in dense graphs. The present proof retains the source's linear PART count, permits long cycles, and adds no short-cycle claim."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/expanded-target-2026-10-17/structural-r176-proof-r1-brief.txt", "line": 436, "text": "The actual BMv2 proofs Sections2.5-2.6,3.3-3.4,4,5 give the hypergraph obstruction, union/halving connectivity, random-sampling amplification, sparse skeletons, complementary path closure, iterative degree reduction and DFS bypass. They are stronger comparators than just log-star in the title. CFS actual Sections3 and5.1 already give saturation-based greedy paths and reservoir closure. Lovasz's original finite decreasing-parameter reconstruction pays polynomial path decomposition. Their use is fully credited."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/expanded-target-2026-10-17/structural-r176-proof-r1-brief.txt", "line": 470, "text": "- CFS: author-hosted journal PDF, received2 October2013/accepted13 May2014, published16 October2014. [0,12051) main statements/full Section2; [12051,23378) Section3 through all reservoir/degree-reduction proof; [31928,44299) Section5 introduction, actual saturation proof Lemma5.1, its combination Lemma5.2, cut-dense theorem and short path proof Lemma5.4, plus beginning5.5; [54140,56269) full Lemma6.3 trimming proof. Remainder of5.5, full random-graph and full dense-graph proofs not claimed read. Crucially saturation was read BEFORE freeze and is expressly credited as paid."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/fresh-structural-discovery-r176/AUTHOR-PROOF.md", "line": 263, "text": "The new assertion is algorithmic: an explicit zero-error expected-polynomial algorithm for the source's full unrestricted graph class. Source181 gives the existence theorem and all structural vertex savings. BM supplies genuine expansion, sampling and iterative path/cycle machinery. CFS already supplies greedy saturation. Lovasz supplies the constructive path operation. Short-cycle algorithms, including LSY, already supply fast explicit partitions with a linear number of leftover edges; they do not bound the total number of cycle parts linearly in dense graphs. The present proof retains the source's linear PART count, permits long cycles, and adds no short-cycle claim."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/structural-r176-proof-r1/REVIEW.md", "line": 131, "text": "Actual BM v2 proofs of the hypergraph routing formulation, union/halving connectivity, robust expansion operations, edge splitting, random-set amplification, sparse skeletons, three-complement closure, DFS bypass, and iterative reduction were read. They explain the source mechanisms but do not eliminate the need to verify the new algorithmic searches. Actual CFS reservoir, cut charging, saturation and path-trimming proofs were read. Actual GGKO main hypotheses and Proposition 6.3 were read: its quasirandom cycle conclusion is not an unrestricted computational replacement. Its full regularity/Hamilton-decomposition ancestry was not followed because it is not used by S176A. Actual AABC v2 maximum-degree-four, even-remainder exchange, and matching-based 2-regular operations were read; a 2-regular part can contain many cycles. They do not establish the required simple-cycle part count by mere reinterpretation. Covers are not partitions."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/fresh-structural-discovery-r177/private/completed/fresh-structural-discovery-r176/AUTHOR-PROOF.md", "line": 263, "text": "The new assertion is algorithmic: an explicit zero-error expected-polynomial algorithm for the source's full unrestricted graph class. Source181 gives the existence theorem and all structural vertex savings. BM supplies genuine expansion, sampling and iterative path/cycle machinery. CFS already supplies greedy saturation. Lovasz supplies the constructive path operation. Short-cycle algorithms, including LSY, already supply fast explicit partitions with a linear number of leftover edges; they do not bound the total number of cycle parts linearly in dense graphs. The present proof retains the source's linear PART count, permits long cycles, and adds no short-cycle claim."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/structural-r176-contribution-r1/private/completed-inputs/AUTHOR-PROOF.md", "line": 263, "text": "The new assertion is algorithmic: an explicit zero-error expected-polynomial algorithm for the source's full unrestricted graph class. Source181 gives the existence theorem and all structural vertex savings. BM supplies genuine expansion, sampling and iterative path/cycle machinery. CFS already supplies greedy saturation. Lovasz supplies the constructive path operation. Short-cycle algorithms, including LSY, already supply fast explicit partitions with a linear number of leftover edges; they do not bound the total number of cycle parts linearly in dense graphs. The present proof retains the source's linear PART count, permits long cycles, and adds no short-cycle claim."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/structural-r176-proof-r1/private/selected/AUTHOR-PROOF.md", "line": 263, "text": "The new assertion is algorithmic: an explicit zero-error expected-polynomial algorithm for the source's full unrestricted graph class. Source181 gives the existence theorem and all structural vertex savings. BM supplies genuine expansion, sampling and iterative path/cycle machinery. CFS already supplies greedy saturation. Lovasz supplies the constructive path operation. Short-cycle algorithms, including LSY, already supply fast explicit partitions with a linear number of leftover edges; they do not bound the total number of cycle parts linearly in dense graphs. The present proof retains the source's linear PART count, permits long cycles, and adds no short-cycle claim."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/fresh-structural-discovery-r137/work/copied-controls-lglwue14/forged-reseal/packet/private/inputs/acceptance-ledger-snapshot.md", "line": 104, "text": "  by combining the existing R016 argument with Leake\u2013Lins\u2013Spitkovsky's"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/fresh-structural-discovery-r137/work/copied-controls-lglwue14/symlink/packet/private/inputs/acceptance-ledger-snapshot.md", "line": 104, "text": "  by combining the existing R016 argument with Leake\u2013Lins\u2013Spitkovsky's"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/fresh-structural-discovery-r137/work/copied-controls-lglwue14/report/packet/private/inputs/acceptance-ledger-snapshot.md", "line": 104, "text": "  by combining the existing R016 argument with Leake\u2013Lins\u2013Spitkovsky's"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/fresh-structural-discovery-r137/work/copied-controls-lglwue14/manifest/packet/private/inputs/acceptance-ledger-snapshot.md", "line": 104, "text": "  by combining the existing R016 argument with Leake\u2013Lins\u2013Spitkovsky's"}, {"path": 