 adaptive cutoff and all entrance conditions, compact-mixture consequence, full finite Fourier subgroup identity, regular part and scaling formulas, uniform near-collision errors and chosen epsilon exponents. Audit any regularity claim for the Green remainder rather than assume it from a formal conditionally summed series. Preserve the scope of source screening as approximation of the infimum, not arbitrary near-minimizer rate/defect preservation. Independently assess contribution using the complete operations. Preserve I134 original-scoped audit and inherited I125 literal cano"}, {"path": "frontier/sources/i136_birational_positivity_discovery/snapshots/frontier/iterations/iteration130-spectral-harmonic-discovery-task.json", "line": 3, "text": "  \"brief\": \"I130 \u2014 Original I127 audit and fresh spectral/harmonic geometry discovery.\\nWork in /home/mj-kang/Documents/Dev/math/openai-proof-research; read AGENTS.md, upstream identity and current ledgers. Eight substantial findings accepted, two remain. User explicitly authorizes T3 subagents and stipulates ALL OpenAI theorems AND lower operations at fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb. No upstream truth audit, contradiction or ex-falso synthesis. External papers are not stipulated. No children, shared edits, staging, commits or publication. Own ONLY frontier/iterations/i130-spectral-harmonic-discovery.md, frontier/sources/i130_spectral_harmonic_discovery/, frontier/experiments/i130_spectral_harmonic_discovery/. Do not bind active I128/I129 outputs.\\n\\nFIRST independently audit all ORIGINAL I127 new paid claims without repairs: N1 Hilbert conditional expectation/sign inequality including extended L2, N2 inverse-mass retention, N3 actual source piecewise pin Lipschitz bound with class and anchor constancy, nominal-length (not anchor-depth) mask derivatives, planar Gamma scope and bounded endpoint-multiplier allowance; complete gamma>3 conditional common-pin retention route; N4 actual Cantor affine-pushforward